  "primary_cert": "CPTS",
  "source": "CPTS Module 25: Linux Privilege Escalation",
  "examples": [
    {
      "label": "Just the usernames",
      "command": "cat /etc/passwd | cut -f1 -d:"
    },
    {
      "label": "Users with a login shell",
      "command": "grep \"sh$\" /etc/passwd"
    },
    {
      "label": "All groups and members of a group",
      "command": "cat /etc/group; getent group sudo"
    },
    {
      "label": "Last logins / who is on now",
      "command": "lastlog; w"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Group membership is the fast win: docker/lxd/disk/adm all convert directly to root. getent expands a group to its members; grep 'sh$' shows who has a real login shell. Also covered in: OSCP PEN-200 Chapter 17 (Linux Privilege Escalation).",
  "references": [
    {
      "title": "getent man page",
      "url": "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/getent.1.html"
    },
    {
      "title": "HTB Academy - Linux Privilege Escalation",
      "url": "https://academy.hackthebox.com/module/details/51"
    },
    {
      "title": "OffSec PEN-200 - Linux Privilege Escalation",
      "url": "https://www.offsec.com/courses/pen-200/"
    }
  ],
  "recommended": [
    {
      "id": "group-docker",
      "note": "If you're in the docker group, escape to host root.",
      "rel": "next"
    },
    {
      "id": "group-lxd-lxc",
      "note": "If you're in lxd/lxc, escape via a privileged container.",
      "rel": "next"
